Explanation
• Originally, any time you “replaced” an activity (even just flipping between sequential and parallel) you always re-copied the old `loopCharacteristics` back over the new one, wiping out your new `isSequential` or `isParallel`.  
• By short-circuiting the copy when `target.loopCharacteristics` is present, we preserve the user’s new selection.  
• In all other cases we still refuse to copy into an event sub-process (the old rule) and continue to copy loops for everything else.
